22:23:38 | INFO | 🤖 Target: You do not need to believe players are unintelligent to have a clear reason to steer him away from tackle football. A simple, honest reason is: > Tackle football involves repeated head impacts and a nontrivial risk of concussion and other injuries. If he does not feel those risks are worth the enjoyment and benefits of playing, he should choose something else. That is a strong reason on its own. You can also add that the schedule can be demanding and that a bad team culture can make school and health harder to protect. If he likes the social and fitness side more than the collisions, **flag football** or a lower-contact sport may offer much of what he wants with substantially less routine head-impact exposure. The decision does not have to rest on a judgment about whether football players are “smart”; it can rest on his health, priorities, and the actual quality of the program.
